# the judge and the boy. 
~ start
Judge: Why hello. You seem lost. 
You: I am not lost.
Judge: Well what are you doing out on the mother prairie? 
You: Going elsewhere, where my dad aint. 
Judge: Heh heh heh. I had a similar inclination at your age, just went about it a different way. Heh heh.
Judge: Tell you what, why don't you tell me where your old pappy is and I'll give him a talking to. I'll tell him no more chores for you, fried donuts every day and you can sleep till noon. 
Judge: Come on, wadya say?
- Tell the pale man where you live. => murder
- Refuse. => flight 

~ flight 
Judge: You don't want to go back eh. Thats your house boy. Soon enough you'll see the world for what it is. The longer it takes, the more you will suffer. 
Judge: I won't try to convince you. I can see your yellow belly.
Judge: But, since I offered you a gift, its only polite that you offer me something, for the sake of propriety of course. I would not ask but manners are so dear to me. 
Judge: What do you have for me boy?
- Im not givin you nothing. 
	Judge: I hate to be uncouth but I won't let you go until I get whats mine. For propriety, you must understand. 
	You: What do you want? I ain't got nothing 'cept the clothes on my back. 
	Judge: You still got yourself. Let me have a look at your eyes and you will be free to go. 
	- Let him => eyes
	- Run
	Narrator: He flicks out his leg and trips you before you can make more than two steps. He holds you up by your shirt. 
	Judge: I HATE BAD MANNERED BOYS. I SEE NOW WHY YOUR PAPPY BEAT YOU. 
	Judge: LOOK INTO MY EYES BOY OR I'LL ROAST YOU OVER THIS HERE FIRE. 
	- Look into his eyes => eyes
	- Shut eyes
		Narrator: He drags you over to the fire and starts to push you into it. 
		- Keep eyes shut. 
			Narrator: He is true to his word. He roasts you til crisp. 
		- Open eyes and look at him => eyes
- Look through pockets. 
	Narrator: You find northing except a dime of stale jerky. 
- Offer service. 
	You: Lemme join your posse. 
=> END

~ eyes
Judge: Heh heh. You got an interstin future before ya. 
Judge: Aahahahh, your great grandson will father the Hydrogen bomb. I think I'll let ya go. 
Judge: Go on now, before I change my mind. 
=> END

~ murder
You: I been heading north for about two days now so the homestead is south that same distance. I doubt hes even home, I bet hes lookin all over for me. 
Judge: No he aint. Hes sittin pretty in a big rockin chair. Come on, you will come with me and we will pay him a visit together.
=> END